help get_value_database
get_value_database

Description: 
Get value of the selected HDL object (variable, signal, wire, reg) at the specified time

Syntax: 
get_value_database  [-radix <arg>] [-time <arg>] [-quiet] [-verbose]
                    <hdl_object>

Returns: 
Returns a string representation of value of a hdl_object

Usage: 
  Name          Description
  -------------------------
  [-radix]      Specifies which radix to use.  Allowed values are: default, 
                dec, bin, oct, hex, unsigned, ascii
  [-time]       simulation time
  [-quiet]      Ignore command errors
  [-verbose]    Suspend message limits during command execution
  <hdl_object>  The hdl_object to retrieve the current value

Categories: 
Simulation
help find_next_wave_value
find_next_wave_value

Description: 
Find next waveform value

Syntax: 
find_next_wave_value  [-wave <arg>] [-radix <arg>] [-match <arg>] [-time <arg>]
                      [-quiet] [-verbose] [<pattern>]

Usage: 
  Name         Description
  ------------------------
  [-wave]      the wave object to search for value
  [-radix]     radix specifies the radix to use for the value pattern. Allowed
               values are: dec, bin, oct,hex, unsigned
  [-match]     match specifies the match location to use for the value 
               pattern. Allowed values are: exact, beginning, end
  [-time]      starting time. The defaul time unit is ns.
  [-quiet]     Ignore command errors
  [-verbose]   Suspend message limits during command execution
  [<pattern>]  value pattern to be search

Categories: 
Waveform
